 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 18172,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2426\" data-start=\"2193\">The <strong data-end=\"2220\" data-start=\"2197\">client-server model</strong> is a network communication framework where a <strong data-end=\"2276\" data-start=\"2266\">client</strong> sends requests to a <strong data-end=\"2307\" data-start=\"2297\">server</strong>, and the server provides the requested services or data. It is widely used in web, database, and file-sharing systems.</p>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"2449\" data-start=\"2433\"><strong data-end=\"2449\" data-start=\"2437\">Working:</strong></h3>\n\n<ol data-end=\"2738\" data-start=\"2451\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2512\" data-start=\"2451\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2512\" data-start=\"2454\"><strong data-end=\"2464\" data-start=\"2454\">Client</strong> initiates communication by sending a request.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2580\" data-start=\"2513\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2580\" data-start=\"2516\"><strong data-end=\"2526\" data-start=\"2516\">Server</strong> listens for incoming connections using socket APIs.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2673\" data-start=\"2581\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2673\" data-start=\"2584\">Once connected, both exchange data through a <strong data-end=\"2655\" data-start=\"2629\">communication protocol</strong> (e.g., TCP/IP).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2738\" data-start=\"2674\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2738\" data-start=\"2677\">After completing the communication, the connection is closed.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"2768\" data-start=\"2745\"><strong data-end=\"2768\" data-start=\"2749\">Key Components:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"2770\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2871\" data-start=\"2770\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2785\" data-start=\"2772\"><strong data-end=\"2783\" data-start=\"2772\">Client:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2871\" data-start=\"2788\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2820\" data-start=\"2788\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2820\" data-start=\"2790\">Sends requests for services.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2871\" data-start=\"2823\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2871\" data-start=\"2825\">Waits for and processes the server&#39;s response.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2976\" data-start=\"2873\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2888\" data-start=\"2875\"><strong data-end=\"2886\" data-start=\"2875\">Server:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2976\" data-start=\"2891\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2923\" data-start=\"2891\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2923\" data-start=\"2893\">Listens for client requests.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2976\" data-start=\"2926\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2976\" data-start=\"2928\">Processes the request and sends back a response.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"2978\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3007\" data-start=\"2980\"><strong data-end=\"3005\" data-start=\"2980\">Communication Medium:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"3010\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3082\" data-start=\"3010\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3082\" data-start=\"3012\">Usually involves <strong data-end=\"3047\" data-start=\"3029\">TCP/IP sockets</strong>, named pipes, or message queues.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"3085\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"3087\">TCP ensures reliable transmission.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3152\" data-start=\"3128\"><strong data-end=\"3152\" data-start=\"3132\">Role of Sockets:</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"3221\" data-start=\"3154\">A <strong data-end=\"3166\" data-start=\"3156\">socket</strong> is an endpoint for communication between two machines.</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3460\" data-start=\"3223\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3308\" data-start=\"3223\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3308\" data-start=\"3225\"><strong data-end=\"3241\" data-start=\"3225\">Server side:</strong> Uses <code data-end=\"3257\" data-start=\"3247\">socket()</code>, <code data-end=\"3267\" data-start=\"3259\">bind()</code>, <code data-end=\"3279\" data-start=\"3269\">listen()</code>, and <code data-end=\"3295\" data-start=\"3285\">accept()</code> functions.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3388\" data-start=\"3309\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3388\" data-start=\"3311\"><strong data-end=\"3327\" data-start=\"3311\">Client side:</strong> Uses <code data-end=\"3343\" data-start=\"3333\">socket()</code> and <code data-end=\"3359\" data-start=\"3348\">connect()</code> to initiate communication.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3460\" data-start=\"3389\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3460\" data-start=\"3391\">Once connected, both can use <code data-end=\"3428\" data-start=\"3420\">read()</code> and <code data-end=\"3442\" data-start=\"3433\">write()</code> to exchange data.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3508\" data-start=\"3467\"><strong data-end=\"3508\" data-start=\"3471\">Example Flow (Using TCP Sockets):</strong></h3>\n\n<pre data-end=\"3650\" data-start=\"3510\">\n\n&nbsp;</pre>\n\n<p><code>// Server Side socket(); &rarr; bind(); &rarr; listen(); &rarr; accept(); &rarr; read()/write() // Client Side socket(); &rarr; connect(); &rarr; read()/write() </code></p>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3674\" data-start=\"3657\"><strong data-end=\"3674\" data-start=\"3661\">Benefits:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3821\" data-start=\"3676\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3714\" data-start=\"3676\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3714\" data-start=\"3678\">Enables <strong data-end=\"3712\" data-start=\"3686\">distributed processing</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3762\" data-start=\"3715\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3762\" data-start=\"3717\">Supports <strong data-end=\"3741\" data-start=\"3726\">scalability</strong> and <strong data-end=\"3760\" data-start=\"3746\">modularity</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3821\" data-start=\"3763\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3821\" data-start=\"3765\">Used in web applications, file transfer, chat apps, etc.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2",
    "PLO3"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"2147\" data-start=\"1983\">Explain the client-server communication model in an operating system. Discuss how it works, the components involved, and the role of sockets in implementing it.</strong></p>\n",
